# Testing Policy (Backend)

- Always write **integration and unit** tests for new features and behavior changes, unless the user explicitly asks not to write tests.
- Unit tests cover pure helpers and isolated service logic (`*.unit-spec.ts`). Integration tests cover HTTP + DB flows (`*.e2e-spec.ts`).
- When changing existing functionality that already has coverage, update those tests so they match the new behavior.
- When adding a new feature, include both layers as part of the work by default: unit for pure/util logic, integration for API behavior.
- Before finishing work that includes tests:
  - Run unit tests with `npm run test:unit`.
  - Run the full integration suite with `npm run test:integration` — not only the newly added tests.
- **Never run tests against production** (`npm run prod`, `npm run prod:ngrok`, `NODE_ENV=production`, live/prod DB or hosts). Run tests only with local/dev or dedicated test setup.
